.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:annotation		ECCE-QM, UPBE0/aug-cc-pVDZ, energy. This calculation shows the nitrogen anion, the atom with one extra electron; the energy of the neutral atom minus the energy of this anion is the electron affinity. The 2p orbitals of nitrogen are half full, one electron in each, so the extra electron has to pair with one of them and feels the repulsion of that electron, and the anion is not more stable than the atom.
